The body is decoded using `decodeJsonJumpTable[dst->type->typeKind]`. If the type is, say, a structure with a LocalizedText member, the body would be decoded as that structure, and the LocalizedText member would be decoded by `LocalizedText_decodeJson`.

This all seems correct. Let me look at the actual crash more carefully. The crash is "Heap-use-after-free READ 8" in `LocalizedText_clear`. This means when `LocalizedText_clear` tries to read `p->locale` or `p->text` (which are `UA_String` structs), the memory has already been freed.

`UA_String` is:
```c
