Actually, `UA_free` just frees the memory block. It doesn't call any cleanup. So if `dst->data` points to a struct that contains pointers to other memory, those other memory blocks are NOT freed by `UA_free(dst->data)`. This would cause a memory leak, not a use-after-free.

