Actually, looking at the `Variant_decodeJson` function:

```c
if(isArray) {
    DecodeEntry entries[3] = {
        {UA_JSONKEY_TYPE, NULL, NULL, false, NULL},
        {UA_JSONKEY_BODY, &dst->data, (decodeJsonSignature) Array_decodeJson, false, NULL},
        ...
    };
    ret = decodeFields(ctx, parseCtx, entries, 2, bodyType);
}
```

`Array_decodeJson` is called with `&dst->data` and `bodyType`. `Array_decodeJson` calls `Array_decodeJson_internal((void**)dst, type, ...)`.

In `Array_decodeJson_internal`:
```c
size_t *p = (size_t*) dst - 1;
*p = length;
```

`dst` is `void**` pointing to `&variant->data`. `(size_t*)dst - 1` = `(size_t*)(&variant->data) - sizeof(size_t)`.

On 64-bit, `sizeof(size_t) = 8`. So this writes to `(char*)&variant->data - 8`, which is `&variant->type`.

This would overwrite `variant->type` with the array length! This is clearly a bug.

